Package: MetaOrdDTA
Type: Package
Title: Meta-Analysis of Ordinal Diagnostic Tests at Multiple Thresholds
Version: 0.1
Date: 2025-02-15
Author: Enzo Cerullo
Maintainer: Enzo Cerullo <enzo.cerullo@bath.edu>
Description: An R package for the meta-analysis and network-meta-analysis of diagnostic and screening tests, optimised for ordinal tests such as questionnaires (with possibly missing threshold data is some or all studies). However, it can also be used for binary and continuous tests (e.g. using the Jones et al model). 
License: GPL-3 + file LICENSE
Imports: Rcpp (>= 1.0.0), R6, cmdstanr, bayesplot, posterior, dplyr, ggplot2, tibble, tictoc, doParallel, foreach, stringr, jsonlite, tidyr, purrr, patchwork, forcats, data.table, digest, gtools, LaplacesDemon, MASS, Matrix, MCMCpack, scales, TruncatedNormal, truncnorm, bridgestan
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppEigen
Suggests: roxygen2, testthat (>= 3.0.0), BayesMVP, BayesMVPsim, BayesMVPtest, RcppParallel
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE, roclets = c("namespace", "rd"))
SystemRequirements: GNU make, C++17
RoxygenNote: 7.3.2
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
